WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.202 --> 00:00:04.934
We usually treat earthquakes as an engineering problem that just tests concrete.

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:09.350
They actually trigger a systemic failure called operational collapse.

3
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.958
Take a Dhaka hospital that survives a tremor perfectly intact on the outside,

4
00:00:14.186 --> 00:00:16.038
but goes entirely dark on the inside.

5
00:00:16.714 --> 00:00:21.350
20 million people live in a city where normal dengue seasons overflow emergency rooms,

6
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:25.894
and mental health capacity is just 0.16 psychiatrists per 100,000 people.

7
00:00:26.378 --> 00:00:30.438
This baseline fragility means non-structural damage becomes the ultimate trigger.

8
00:00:30.922 --> 00:00:36.646
Snapped oxygen lines, failed generators, and cracked stairwells force a structurally sound hospital to shut down.

9
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.366
This operational collapse unfolds in waves.

10
00:00:39.754 --> 00:00:42.022
First, immediate physical injuries go untreated.

11
00:00:42.378 --> 00:00:46.214
Then the collapse cascades into public health failures and sanitation breakdowns.

12
00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:50.150
Finally, unmanageable psychological distress paralyzes the community.

13
00:00:50.602 --> 00:00:53.990
And when a city's health system fails, its workforce instantly follows.

14
00:00:54.538 --> 00:00:58.918
Factories miss export deadlines, business continuity breaks, and the broader economy shatters.

15
00:00:59.306 --> 00:01:02.918
So that structurally sound darkened hospital isn't just a medical failure.

16
00:01:03.274 --> 00:01:06.278
It is a guaranteed economic shutdown for the entire city.

17
00:01:06.794 --> 00:01:09.766
Human in purpose. Systemic in method. Protective in outcome.
